detector_raw:
{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "What is the objective of this packing plan — are we minimizing the number of containers used, maximizing the total weight (or total units) of goods shipped, or something else?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding the optimization objective, presenting mutually exclusive options for one decision."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Do we have to ship all available goods (i.e., use up all 120 A, 90 B, 300 C, 90 D, 120 E), or is it acceptable to leave some goods unshipped as long as the containers we do use satisfy the rules?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether all goods must be shipped or if leaving some unshipped is acceptable."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a fixed number of containers available to choose from, or is the number of containers we can use unlimited (i.e., we just decide how many to open)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the constraint on the number of containers, presenting a binary choice between fixed and unlimited."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there a minimum total amount of goods that must be shipped (for example, a required tonnage or a required number of units), or is it acceptable to ship nothing at all (zero containers) if that is the best solution?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether a minimum shipment quantity is required or if zero shipment is allowed."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Are the goods units indivisible (each unit must be assigned whole to a single container, so counts are integers), or can units be split fractionally across containers?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the divisibility of goods units."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any limit on how many units of a single goods type can go into one container (for example, a per-container cap on type A or type C), or is the only per-container restriction the 18–60 ton weight range and the minimum of 12 units of type D?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding per-container unit limits versus weight/unit minimums."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "For the rule \"if a container contains any type A then it must also contain at least one type C\" — does the type C unit(s) required in that container count toward the container's weight and toward the total C availability, just like any other C unit (i.e., there is no separate \"free\" C allowance)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding whether the required type C units count toward weight and availability constraints."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The 18-ton minimum and 60-ton maximum per container — are these strict (i.e., a container must weigh strictly more than 18 tons and strictly less than 60 tons), or are they inclusive (a container weighing exactly 18 tons or exactly 60 tons is allowed)?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks for a single policy choice regarding whether the weight limits are strict or inclusive, which constitutes one semantically independent question."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "The \"at least 12 units of type D\" per container — does this apply to every container that is used (including a container that holds only D and other types), or only to containers that contain at least one unit of type D?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single clarification question regarding the scope of a constraint, presenting two mutually exclusive options for the same policy rule."
}

{
  "action": "question",
  "question_count": 1,
  "is_atomic": true,
  "atomic_questions": [
    "Is there any other requirement or rule I should know about that I haven't asked yet — for example, a requirement that each container must contain at least one unit of every goods type, a limit on the number of containers, or a requirement that specific goods must be shipped together?"
  ],
  "rationale": "The response asks a single open-ended question about whether any other requirements exist, using examples to illustrate the type of information sought. It does not ask for separate answers to the examples, but rather for any additional rules."
}
